<div class="page-head"><div><h1>Site settings</h1>
  <p class="small" style="margin:4px 0 0">Support inbox and the built-in live-chat widget shown on every page.</p></div></div>

<% if (it.ok) { %><div class="notice notice-ok">Site settings saved.</div><% } %>

<div class="grid grid-mail-split">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Support</h3></div>
    <form method="post" action="/admin/site">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= it.csrf %>">
      <div class="field"><label for="supportEmail">Support email</label>
        <input class="input" id="supportEmail" name="supportEmail" type="email" value="<%= it.site.supportEmail %>" placeholder="marketedgesupport@gmail.com" required>
        <div class="hint">Contact-form messages are forwarded to this inbox, and it's the reply address clients see.</div></div>
      <button class="btn btn-primary btn-block btn-sm">Save settings</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Live chat — built-in</h3></div>
    <p class="small" style="margin:0">The chat widget is part of the website itself — no external account,
      no API key, no third-party dashboard. The bubble shows on <b>every page</b> (public site, login,
      client dashboard and this admin console).</p>
    <ul class="small" style="margin:10px 0 0;padding-left:18px;line-height:1.7">
      <li>Guests send with a name (email optional); signed-in clients chat from their account.</li>
      <li>Conversations land in <a href="/admin/chat">People → Live chat</a> with an unread counter.</li>
      <li>Replies appear in the client's widget within ~4 seconds; registered users also get a
        notification bell entry.</li>
    </ul>
    <a class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" href="/admin/chat" style="margin-top:12px">Open the chat inbox</a>
  </div>
</div>
